# nomic-embed-v2-moe-bf16.recipe -- nomic-embed-text-v2-moe from the HF checkpoint, as the
# nomicbert plugin serves it.
#
#   rad-convert /data --recipe data/recipes/nomic-embed-v2-moe-bf16.recipe -o nomic.rad
#
# The checkpoint stores every tensor f32 (config.json says torch_dtype float32). The plugin runs
# the linears, the token table and the token-type table in bf16 and keeps norms and biases f32, so
# this recipe casts exactly the weights that plugin declares bf16. Without it rad-convert refuses
# the checkpoint at declare: a declare-time bf16 weight cannot hold an f32 checkpoint's codes.
#
# token_type.weight is bf16 because libr4d's table_add_bf16 reads a bf16 table; libref's and
# libavx's table_add read any dtype the tensor carries, so the same container serves all three.
# The checkpoint's mlp.experts.bias tensors are not mapped by the plugin at all and do not appear
# in the plan.

token_embd.weight             cast  dtype=bf16
token_type.weight             cast  dtype=bf16
blk.*.attn_qkv.weight         cast  dtype=bf16
blk.*.attn_out.weight         cast  dtype=bf16
blk.*.ffn_fc1.weight          cast  dtype=bf16
blk.*.ffn_fc2.weight          cast  dtype=bf16
blk.*.ffn_router.weight       cast  dtype=bf16
blk.*.ffn_exp_w1.*.weight     cast  dtype=bf16
blk.*.ffn_exp_w2.*.weight     cast  dtype=bf16
